{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>Better.</b> It will be better for one who is not wise to hear a wise man's rebuke of him, and it will benefit him more. And if the rebuke benefits, all the more so words of wisdom. And the meaning is that even the rebuke of a wise man who is angry is more beneficial, and the soul will take pleasure in it more than in the song of fools."], :book :ecclesiastes, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 7, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Wikisource" "https://he.wikisource.org/wiki/%D7%90%D7%91%D7%9F_%D7%A2%D7%96%D7%A8%D7%90_%D7%A2%D7%9C_%D7%A7%D7%94%D7%9C%D7%AA"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:28:00.475647698Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}